WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:05.500
Lucas Black knows how to make an exit - and
so does NCIS: New Orleans.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:08.100
Heads up - major spoilers ahead.

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:14.240
During the sixth episode of Season Six, called
"Matthew 5:9," Black's character Special Agent

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:19.110
Christopher LaSalle died after sustaining
gunshot wounds to his arm and stomach while

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:21.260
on a mission to avenge the death of his brother.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:26.580
It's not easy to say goodbye to a key character
after six seasons, but it's comforting to

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:31.669
know that Black reportedly didn't depart from
NCIS: New Orleans on a whim or because of

00:00:31.669 --> 00:00:33.880
any behind-the-scenes drama no one knew about.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.120
Instead, Black exited the procedural for a
very important reason: to spend more time

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:39.800
with family.

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:44.760
In a video uploaded to the NCIS: New Orleans
YouTube channel, Black, who is married with

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:48.760
three children, explained his decision to
part ways with the CBS series.

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:52.800
He admitted that while the show has been,
quote, "so good to [him] over the years,"

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:54.620
the schedule wasn't always easy.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:01:00.080
"There's a lot of priorities in my life that
get sacrificed for me to be here.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:03.580
But it's time for me to focus on those priorities."

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:08.650
It may be tough for fans to accept a beloved
star has other priorities, but nothing but

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:12.260
love and support has surrounded Black's dramatic
exit from the show.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:16.700
According to TV Insider, the NCIS: New Orleans
showrunners said in a statement,

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:21.560
"We had an amazing run with Lucas Black and
he has been such an important part of our

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:23.440
NCIS: New Orleans team.

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:27.400
We are sad to see him go, but happy he will
have more time to spend with his family."

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:33.440
High-profile stars might sometimes use "family"
as a fake excuse to exit an unwanted situation,

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:36.980
but Black's co-workers seem convinced that
his reasons are genuine.

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:37.480
C.C.H.

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:42.000
Pounder, who plays medical examiner Loretta
Wade, said in a video released by the show

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:45.460
that Black wasn't all that concerned with
the idea of being a Hollywood star.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:52.200
"The most important thing is to be a family
man and I think he's just not over all the

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:52.860
other choices."

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:57.900
Black, who according to CBS, earned his first
film role when he was 11, has mainly worked

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:00.060
on NCIS over the last six years.

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:04.580
Newsweek previously speculated that Black
might be leaving the show to free up time

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:09.250
for other on-screen ventures - like future
installments of the Fast &amp; Furious franchise,

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:13.100
in which he plays Tokyo-based American street
racer Sean Boswell.

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:19.460
Black last appeared in 2015's Furious 7 and
was also in 2006's The Fast and the Furious:

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:20.200
Tokyo Drift.

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:25.280
Rumors of his casting in Fast &amp; Furious 9
have swirled for several years, but Black

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:28.820
was also expected to appear in the eighth
movie in the franchise and didn't.

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:33.840
While it's not clear yet whether Black will
appear in Fast &amp; Furious 9, it's also unknown

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:38.080
whether any movie casting would have taken
him away from NCIS: New Orleans.

00:02:38.349 --> 00:02:42.659
As for what's next for the actor, Black didn't
offer any hints about future movie roles in

00:02:42.659 --> 00:02:45.709
his own video posted to Twitter after the
death of LaSalle.

00:02:45.709 --> 00:02:50.380
Instead, he chose to focus on expressing gratitude
for fans for all of their love and support.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:55.700
"You were there to celebrate the victories
and to pick me up when I needed it and I appreciate

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:56.200
that."

00:02:56.540 --> 00:03:01.359
The actor also indicated he would miss playing
LaSalle, and remains incredibly thankful for

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:03.780
the time he spent on NCIS: New Orleans.

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:07.920
He went on to say that he, quote, "learned
a lot about what the first responders do,"

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:10.220
and that he supports and respects the military.

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:11.420
"A chapter has ended.

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:13.220
What a great journey it was.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.140
Thank you guys so much.

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:16.120
May God bless you."

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:21.230
So far, much of NCIS: New Orleans season 6
has been about LaSalle's search for his missing

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:26.220
brother - whom he then discovers is dead - and
his team's attempts to help him in his quest.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:31.079
It's not clear where that plot will go after
LaSalle's death - and a preview of the next

00:03:31.079 --> 00:03:38.049
episode of the show, excitingly titled "Boom-Boom-Boom-Boom,"
only teases a new storyline involving bombs

00:03:38.049 --> 00:03:38.660
in the city.

00:03:39.049 --> 00:03:45.120
However, NCIS: New Orleans star Necar Zadegan,
who plays Special Agent Hannah Khoury, promised

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:48.160
that LaSalle's character would have a major
effect on the show.

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:51.340
"LaSalle's character was such a big, important
character to the show.

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:55.720
It does have a big impact on the team in terms
of not just the relationship but personal

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:56.500
stories."

00:03:56.729 --> 00:04:02.719
Star Scott Bakula who portrays Supervisory
Special Agent Dwayne "King" Pride, also revealed

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:05.989
that LaSalle's death means change for NCIS:
New Orleans.

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:11.680
"We're off on a big, dramatic change for our
world here for season 6."

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:17.520
While the NCIS franchise is still going strong,
ratings for NCIS: New Orleans have sadly been

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:20.040
declining, according to TV By The Numbers.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:24.410
Though it's likely upsetting for fans of the
actor, LaSalle's exit just might give the

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:28.540
show a shot in the arm for fresh plot lines
for the rest of the season and beyond.

